      },
      "message": "Add X-COM Serial2CAN bridge with tests, evidence and ASPICE report\n\nNew X-Verse/ folder for Thinking CAPs X-Verse integration components.\nX-Verse/bridges/serial2can bridges serial SLCAN ECUs (ThreadX AZ3166)\nto an X-Verse CAN bus (SocketCAN vcan0 or rootless udp_multicast), so\nthe unchanged Zenoh2CAN bridge and other tools see them as CAN nodes.\n\n- Per-port ID filters, serial-to-serial fan-out, Lawicell handshake,\n  hot-plug reconnect, bounded TX queues, echo suppression for looping\n  buses, close (C) to every ECU on shutdown, JSON statistics\n- 302 host tests (codec units, pseudo-terminal ECU integration,\n  robustness, CLI); hardware check on the AZ3166; live X-Verse + CARLA\n  run through Zenoh2CAN -> Serial2CAN -> AZ3166\n- ASPICE SWE.1-SWE.6 work products, PlantUML views and a generator for\n  the HTML report (ruff/mypy clean, 95% line / 90% branch coverage)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
